WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.240 --> 00:00:01.920
(pen scratching)
(classical violin music)

00:00:01.920 --> 00:00:04.520
- [Woman] People try to place you in a box

00:00:04.520 --> 00:00:06.670
when you're a black writer

00:00:06.670 --> 00:00:10.580
as if other audiences
can't enjoy your material.

00:00:10.580 --> 00:00:12.060
- It's like we just put our head down

00:00:12.060 --> 00:00:15.600
and written 44 books over
the span of 11 years.

00:00:15.600 --> 00:00:17.600
We looked up and we're the youngest

00:00:17.600 --> 00:00:20.040
African-American novelists, as a couple,

00:00:20.040 --> 00:00:22.570
to make the New York Times.

00:00:22.570 --> 00:00:24.208
It changed our life.

00:00:24.208 --> 00:00:28.279
(energetic classical violin music)

00:00:28.279 --> 00:00:30.430
(energetic piano music)

00:00:30.430 --> 00:00:34.242
We from Flint, in particular
I'm from the 5th Ward of Flint.

00:00:34.242 --> 00:00:35.800
It's one of the roughest neighborhoods.

00:00:35.800 --> 00:00:36.820
It's dog eat dog.

00:00:37.970 --> 00:00:40.600
But I love it because it taught me how to

00:00:40.600 --> 00:00:41.650
come from the bottom.

00:00:42.500 --> 00:00:45.360
Our city is dark but once you figure out

00:00:45.360 --> 00:00:47.130
how to utilize that darkness,

00:00:47.130 --> 00:00:48.850
that's when you become great.

00:00:48.850 --> 00:00:51.830
- We're writing about the things

00:00:51.830 --> 00:00:53.840
that America covers up.

00:00:53.840 --> 00:00:56.070
The neighborhoods that you don't see

00:00:56.070 --> 00:00:57.840
and that you never hear about.

00:00:57.840 --> 00:00:59.640
- [Jaquavis] Our books are us.

00:00:59.640 --> 00:01:01.290
It's black America in a nutshell.

00:01:03.212 --> 00:01:04.080
(fast piano music)
(sirens wailing)

00:01:04.080 --> 00:01:07.420
Well when we met each other
our mutual passion was writing.

00:01:07.420 --> 00:01:08.950
- [Ashley] I was 15 years old.

00:01:08.950 --> 00:01:12.050
- Fell in love and, you know,
she ended up becoming my wife.

00:01:13.130 --> 00:01:13.963
- We just wrote.
(gentle clacking)

00:01:13.963 --> 00:01:15.280
We barely slept, we barely ate,

00:01:15.280 --> 00:01:17.140
we definitely didn't leave the house.

00:01:17.140 --> 00:01:20.190
There was no formula for it.
(sharp cha-chinging)

00:01:20.190 --> 00:01:21.480
Now we use systems.

00:01:21.480 --> 00:01:24.260
We have a system where we
write every single thought

00:01:24.260 --> 00:01:27.950
on Post-its and we stick them
anywhere around the house.

00:01:27.950 --> 00:01:29.990
We feel like our words are worth dollars.

00:01:29.990 --> 00:01:31.230
So anytime you forget
(sharp cha-chinging)

00:01:31.230 --> 00:01:34.020
something it's like flushing
money down the toilet,

00:01:34.020 --> 00:01:36.790
so we don't ever want to ever
let a thought pass us by.

00:01:38.066 --> 00:01:39.570
(somber piano music)

00:01:39.570 --> 00:01:44.070
I love when I walk into a
bookstore, and I see The Cartel

00:01:44.070 --> 00:01:46.240
sitting next to a James Patterson book

00:01:46.240 --> 00:01:48.503
because that's where it belongs.

00:01:48.503 --> 00:01:50.240
I remember in the beginning
I would go in a bookstore

00:01:50.240 --> 00:01:52.110
and move the books to the front.

00:01:52.110 --> 00:01:55.740
It's important to erase
that street fiction moniker.

00:01:55.740 --> 00:01:57.280
When you label something street fiction

00:01:57.280 --> 00:01:59.310
you immediately put it in a small section

00:01:59.310 --> 00:02:02.330
in the bookstore, and only certain people

00:02:02.330 --> 00:02:03.810
will go to that section.

00:02:03.810 --> 00:02:06.300
We're very fortunate to
have broken out of that box,

00:02:06.300 --> 00:02:08.640
and we hope that now we've opened the door

00:02:08.640 --> 00:02:10.560
that now other black writers can come

00:02:10.560 --> 00:02:14.090
through that door behind us.
(crowd cheering)

00:02:14.090 --> 00:02:15.910
- [Jaquavis] We don't wanna
be great for this lifetime,

00:02:15.910 --> 00:02:18.290
we wanna be great for
five generations down.

00:02:19.158 --> 00:02:20.660
Back then we was chasing checks,

00:02:20.660 --> 00:02:22.470
now we're chasing history.

00:02:22.470 --> 00:02:27.470
(soft piano music)
(soft clicking)

